:INFO
Art. 40 Data retention requirements
1 The sponsor must retain all data concerning the clinical trial until the expiry date of the last series of devices used in the trial, but for a minimum of ten years following the completion or premature termination of the clinical trial. The retention period for implantable devices is at least 15 years.
2 The investigator must retain all documents required to identify and provide post-trial care to participants, as well as all other original data, for at least ten years after the completion or premature termination of the clinical trial. The retention period for implantable devices is at least 15 years.

